{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 10, :comments ["<b>And it came to pass, when</b> etc. The reason it says three times <b>his mother's brother</b> seemingly without need is to say that all his actions were on account of his being his mother's brother, and for his mother's honor. Or it may be on account of the suspicion that they might see him doing kindness with Rachel while he was a foreign man — therefore he would state from his mouth the reason for the matter: when he saw Rachel he said ״daughter of Laban his mother's brother״, the sheep of Laban his mother's brother, and at the time of watering as well — thereby he removed from himself any suspicion of impropriety. And at the time he kissed her he did not say it, for he had already said it; and further, his weeping would proclaim about him that they were relatives." "<b>Further,</b> it intends according to the statement of our Sages of blessed memory (Avodah Zarah 26a) that the nations do not raise up or bring down [i.e., their actions are not Divinely assisted] — therefore it says <b>and he watered the sheep of Laban</b>, and the reason is (Proverbs 14:34) ״the kindness of peoples,״ for on account of their being his mother's brother, for his mother's honor, he watered [them]."], :book :genesis, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 29, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T19:44:28.669443899Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}